INVARIANT — Evidence-only resume generation
============================================

No generated word may appear in the PDF unless it can be traced to:

  1. AC fact          (YAML fact field on a selected accomplishment)
  2. AC variant       (pre-authored variant text on a selected AC)
  3. AC facet         (facet phrase/keywords on a selected AC)
  4. Skills evidence  (skill listed in skills_audit with covered: true)
  5. Profile metadata (name, contact, education, role titles, dates, locations)

Forbidden:

  - LLM rewrite of bullets at PDF generation time
  - Suffix injection ("with X and Y" appended to bullets)
  - Skills not backed by selected AC or project evidence
  - Invented metrics, technologies, or employers

Enforcement:

  scripts/ac-invariant.mjs     — traces every emitted token to evidence
  scripts/ac-resume-score.mjs    — Resume Confidence Score (north star)
  scripts/ac-beam.mjs            — generates candidates; gate picks best

Beam search disqualifies INVARIANT violations. The gate scores; it does not kill the build.
Ship the highest-scoring candidate that passes INVARIANT.
